WEBVTT

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:34.050
This tale is a work of pure fiction

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:37.830
<b> June 02, 1582 {ts}</b>

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:37.830
<b> Kyoto Honno Temple {ts}</b>

00:01:57.610 --> 00:01:58.980
Make haste.

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:02.160
More of Akechi's men shall come.

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:20.090
I shall seek the other intruder.

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:23.480
Farewell.

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:34.460
We flee Kyoto now.

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:36.370
Allow me shelter, aye?

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:41.470
Make haste, Furusa!

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:06.640
Ne'er again, shall I hear the shrill laughter of Milord.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:14.680
Such is commonplace in this era of war.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:23.260
Woe, for my fate takes precedence over the dread that is Milord's passing.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:36.590
Milord, one day, shall I prepare ye tea in the afterlife.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.580
<b> Mixed Messages {ts}</b>

00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:52.180
Father!

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:53.100
Father!

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:55.060
Father!

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.030
What is amiss, Tadaoki?

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:00.660
I've received tidings from General Akechi!

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:04.320
He claims his forces to have murdered Milord at Honno Temple!

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:10.430
He requests for our clan to join in his rebellion!

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:11.580
Be this absolute?!

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:14.870
The messenger claims to have witnessed Honno Temple burning.

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:18.210
Neither was he certain of Milord's whereabouts.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:24.500
General Akechi has since returned to Sakamoto Castle.

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:27.760
Father, we must purge the rebellious cretin that is Akechi Mitsuhide!

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:30.520
Our clans are now related through you and his daughter!

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:32.150
Aware of this, I am!

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:35.210
Though Milady Tama be the daughter of Mitsuhide...

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:36.110
I shan't yield! {shikashi}

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:46.850
The loyalty of our clan aligns itself to Milord's overall!

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:51.790
Nevertheless, I alone shall see to swift justice administered to Mitsuhide!

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:58.170
Halt, my son!

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:16.520
The merchants of Sakai, myself included, owe a great deal to Milord.

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:26.050
Were one to rebel against Milord, Sakai merchants would henceforth cease assistance to such a rebel.

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:29.450
Master Senno had known of this plot.

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:43.880
There be more than pulp to this fruit.

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:49.890
We shan't take risk with allegiance, for our very clan may be purged as well.

00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:59.860
Only Generals Shibata, Hashiba, and Tokugawa retain great influence.{Drama please check this line}

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:07.360
Were we to refuse assistance to Akechi, which of these three shall topple him? {until misetemorau}

00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:11.940
The nation shall change, regardless the victor.

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:16.370
The embodiment of values the people hold shall change as well. {until kachi wo oku kana}

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:19.970
<b> June 03, 1582 {ts}</b>

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:19.970
<b> Kamikuze Manor Furuta's Residence {ts}</b>

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:25.110
Milord has been worn by the harsh road.

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:29.260
They may not befit Milord, but do bear with them.

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:32.660
'Tis a fine robe of olive.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:35.680
Indeed they befit me not, my gratitude to ye.

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:42.090
A fine woman, Furusa.

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:45.150
Ye be unworthy of so fine a woman.

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:48.820
Delicate, akin to the lips of a lass.

00:06:54.700 --> 00:07:00.320
Nameless is this craft, though the delicate nature of such a tea jar is striking.

00:07:07.010 --> 00:07:10.210
Indeed, akin to the lips of a lass...

00:07:10.210 --> 00:07:13.030
Such lips feature this faint hue of crimson.

00:07:13.640 --> 00:07:15.760
'Tis the Seitaka tea jar.

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:22.230
The very beauty of its slender visage may triumph the uniformity of the Triumvirate.

00:07:23.980 --> 00:07:26.450
Do be silent over its whereabouts.

00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:30.030
'Twas not awarded by Milord before others.

00:07:33.490 --> 00:07:39.870
Milord's passing begs the question of his vassal's loyalties.

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:45.590
Peculiar...

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:53.930
This very tea jar may displace my very wares of virtue, yet... {until nano ni}

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:56.640
absent, is the joy of possession.

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:03.530
I feel not the joy akin to possessing the Hiragumo's shattered lid.

00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:05.770
Well... {sate}

00:08:06.980 --> 00:08:08.790
Begs the question, indeed.

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:12.320
I must consider my own welfare henceforth.

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:16.460
Shall I serve General Akechi, or defend my clan?

00:08:17.610 --> 00:08:20.960
Regardless, the nation shall be divided once more.

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:26.920
The men are likely to serve the decorated warrior that is Shibata Katsuie. {until katsiue}

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:30.090
Given the circumstances, serving him may be wisest, yet...

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:35.970
"He shows little promise," imply ye, aye?

00:08:37.170 --> 00:08:39.050
I imply naught...

00:08:39.050 --> 00:08:41.980
General Shibata be absent of finesse and charisma.

00:08:42.260 --> 00:08:46.120
Were I not of Oda, prefer the company of General Akechi.

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:48.820
Shibata's character is simply...

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:54.490
He knows naught but speech and gestures of brawn and strength.

00:08:56.320 --> 00:09:00.630
General Shibata's seated posture is widened from others so, {until hiraki}

00:09:00.630 --> 00:09:03.210
where the posture itself gives emphasis to his crotch.

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:04.930
Indeed, it does. {sou sou}

00:09:04.930 --> 00:09:07.340
Were I to comment on General Shibata's character...

00:09:07.340 --> 00:09:10.560
he is naught but uncouth brute of pomposity. {i think two people speak here - check}

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:13.380
Uncouth, yet a most befitting description.

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:21.700
I shall go to Ibaraki Castle, and return with Brother.

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:23.980
Your brother has not my trust.

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:30.520
Were he to serve Akechi, 'twould see personally to my death.

00:09:33.530 --> 00:09:38.020
I shall return to Gifu, and contemplate upon servitude to another.

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:40.030
Do escort me to the border.

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:50.040
Lord Nagamasu, I shan't serve any but Milord's clan!

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:51.780
'Tis an era of war!

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:55.080
I shan't loathe ye for servitude to Akechi.

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:56.800
Though... {daga sono toki wa}

00:09:58.490 --> 00:10:01.540
ye shall be my foe to fall.

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:16.790
Whereof Milord?

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:17.830
Milord relieves himself. {habakari e}

00:10:17.830 --> 00:10:19.700
Men guard the perimeter as well.

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:25.280
Akechi dared a rebellion in our respite... {until muhon to wa}

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:30.290
Milord's assistance to the Oda's shall deem him a foe.

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:33.000
We number a mere 34.

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:36.360
Repelling foes, be it Akechi's men or others, would prove difficult.

00:10:36.920 --> 00:10:38.340
Aware, am I!

00:10:45.260 --> 00:10:49.270
I must cure the frequency of anxiety's influence over my bowels. {until naosaneba}

00:10:52.580 --> 00:10:56.360
How shall we act through this incident, henceforth? {from dousuru until kirinukenu}

00:10:57.700 --> 00:11:02.370
Withstand a millennia desiring peace, and peace ye may have post-millennia. {until arimasenu}

00:11:10.280 --> 00:11:12.500
We shall return to Mikawa.

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:18.640
Akechi shan't assault one akin to his ideals. {until hitoshii}

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:21.470
Milord shall retain faith in Akechi's honor?

00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:29.870
The best route to Mikawa runs through Iga's domain.

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:34.980
Once within, I shall rally men of Iga and Kouga to our aid.

00:11:35.490 --> 00:11:37.050
See to it, Hanzo.

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:50.860
I place faith in the truth of the words ye uttered that night, General Akechi.

00:11:58.930 --> 00:12:01.050
General Hidenaga, 'tis urgent! {until moshiagemasu}

00:12:01.550 --> 00:12:05.000
A messenger of General Akechi's has arrived.

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:07.510
He brings urgent tidings from the General.

00:12:07.510 --> 00:12:10.580
No other need know of this.

00:12:14.060 --> 00:12:18.960
Two nights prior, Milord traveled to Honno Temple and saw to the death of Oda Nobunaga. {until uchi}

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:25.520
If possible, Milord requests for General Hashiba's allegiance, henceforth.

00:12:26.530 --> 00:12:31.460
Milord desires to unify the nation together with General Hashiba.

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:50.790
General Akechi fulfilled our expectations, Brother.

00:13:20.090 --> 00:13:22.670
General Akechi put Milord to death?!

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:30.640
From where, came this letter?

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:35.100
'Twas a messenger of Akechi, captured en-route to the Mori's.

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:52.180
These tidings be akin to an Emperor's passing!

00:13:52.180 --> 00:13:55.480
Were the Mori's to learn of Milord's death, they would refute peace, {until dokoroka}

00:13:55.480 --> 00:13:59.920
and ally themselves with Akechi to entrap our forces in Chugoku!

00:13:59.920 --> 00:14:02.130
How proceed the negotiations?

00:14:02.130 --> 00:14:05.910
That which remains is the seal of Mori Terumoto.

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:10.140
Dependent, however, on whether or not he has learned of Milord's passing.

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:14.640
Then see to Mori's seal, before he learns of Milord's passing.

00:14:20.650 --> 00:14:24.500
Given these tidings, press not for any binding conditions.

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:29.320
Hasten the withdrawal of our forces for Himeji Castle, where Brother awaits.

00:14:29.810 --> 00:14:31.960
General, why press for retreat?

00:14:31.960 --> 00:14:38.090
Are we not to await General Hashiba's return before withdraw-

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:39.330
Precious time shall be lost! {soredewa osoi}

00:14:40.260 --> 00:14:43.240
Have a warrior of stature similar to my brother's lead. {until juubun}

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:46.820
Alert not the Mori's of our withdrawal, and have the men prepare to depart.

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:47.840
Aye!

00:14:57.400 --> 00:15:01.860
Ye remain calm, regardless of these morbid tidings.

00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:09.610
Concerned for my brother, when he learns of General Akechi's rebellion.

00:15:09.610 --> 00:15:12.960
He may cave and weep over the loss of Milord.

00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:16.860
General Kuroda, I would have ye remain calm as well.

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:25.410
<b> June 04, 1582 {ts}</b>

00:15:24.460 --> 00:15:25.660
General Gamo! {moushiagemasu}

00:15:25.660 --> 00:15:28.330
Akechi's forces shall arrive momentarily!

00:15:28.330 --> 00:15:32.610
'Twas I, whom Milord had granted title of "Ward" over the grand Azuchi Castle... {until katahide}

00:15:33.980 --> 00:15:38.640
and besmirched, the name of Gamo Katahide, to set fire to my care!

00:15:39.010 --> 00:15:42.200
Leave the treasures, and prepare for withdrawal!

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:46.150
Where is my son, Matsuhide? {until izuko}

00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:55.910
M-Milord?!

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:06.170
Father, I have returned.

00:16:06.640 --> 00:16:12.180
As Milord's son through marriage, I sought to spare his horse and arms from Akechi's men.

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:15.570
The armor I adorn is all that remains of Milord's ambition.

00:16:16.060 --> 00:16:21.140
Intend to display to Akechi of Milord's legacy through this attire.

00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:30.380
Dwell not on the memory of Milord, and persevere now.

00:16:31.860 --> 00:16:36.650
Otherwise, our own clan shall fall to the chaos which follows.

00:16:41.450 --> 00:16:45.460
Indebted too great to forsake the memory of Milord.

00:16:54.080 --> 00:17:00.690
From this day, henceforth, Milord Akechi Mitsuhide has reign over the 66 provinces of the realm.

00:17:00.690 --> 00:17:02.800
Milord is Lord of the Realm! {tenkabito ni araseraru}

00:17:05.730 --> 00:17:08.310
My gratitude for exhausted efforts.

00:17:09.900 --> 00:17:12.890
The coward that is Gamo Katahide fled before our forces!

00:17:12.890 --> 00:17:18.860
All that remains in the keep are the treasures accrued by Nobunaga!

00:17:19.710 --> 00:17:21.760
Milord, nay...{drama check timing}

00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:25.430
The Lord of the Realm shall see to the distribution of treasures amongst his own.

00:17:28.310 --> 00:17:32.210
Though we failed to secure the heads of the Nobunaga and his heir,

00:17:32.210 --> 00:17:34.730
certain, am I, of his passing. {until hakondeoru}

00:17:34.730 --> 00:17:37.190
Though, his kin and vassals do remain.

00:17:37.190 --> 00:17:42.430
We are certain to do battle against the likes of Shibata Katsuie.

00:17:42.430 --> 00:17:44.350
Aye, Milord.

00:17:44.910 --> 00:17:49.680
Men, we shan't savor the brew of victory until taking Shibata's head. {until goichido}

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:01.780
I shall salvage all.

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:05.840
Even this gaudy castle, from the base until its keep,

00:18:05.840 --> 00:18:08.960
I shall salvage everything of that tyrant's creation.

00:18:10.890 --> 00:18:14.590
The realm shall be reborn under my ideal.

00:18:15.310 --> 00:18:16.130
Milord!

00:18:16.690 --> 00:18:17.940
What is amiss?

00:18:17.940 --> 00:18:20.050
We've received word from Tango!

00:18:21.770 --> 00:18:26.470
Hosokawa Tadaoki and Fujitaka have taken tonsures. {until yoshi}

00:18:26.470 --> 00:18:30.310
They intend ally themselves not between Milord nor any other.

00:18:30.310 --> 00:18:31.790
Inconceivable!

00:18:33.110 --> 00:18:35.420
The Hosokawas are relatives of Milord!

00:18:36.110 --> 00:18:38.420
Sworn allies, even!

00:18:39.740 --> 00:18:42.230
Is there word from any other?

00:18:42.230 --> 00:18:45.410
Not at present, Milord.

00:18:50.760 --> 00:18:51.420
Milord...

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:57.470
I shan't allow anxiety's hold...

00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:09.470
Others have learned not of the death of the tyrant, Nobunaga.

00:19:14.900 --> 00:19:18.950
Though, certain men should know...

00:19:19.980 --> 00:19:26.790
that my aesthetic ideals for the era to come surpasses the ambitions of a tyrant.

00:19:27.920 --> 00:19:31.700
<b> June 05, 1582 {ts}</b>

00:19:31.740 --> 00:19:33.800
"Tidings of a messenger from Kyoto entails {until yoreba}

00:19:33.800 --> 00:19:41.700
Milord and Lord Nobutada fled from Kyoto unscathed, and into the Omi Province.

00:19:42.470 --> 00:19:50.170
Though we rejoice, our situation worsens, and my forces have left the Chugoku region to fortify Himeji Castle. {until naki you}

00:19:50.980 --> 00:19:56.600
To my fellow, Furuta Sasuke, be well in health."

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:00.990
'Twas received from Bizen, these tidings?

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:06.360
Upon learning of Akechi's rebellion, I sent multiple letters requesting validity on this matter,

00:20:06.360 --> 00:20:08.820
and General Hashiba's was the first to arrive.

00:20:10.440 --> 00:20:13.110
General Akechi's had arrived as well.

00:20:13.110 --> 00:20:16.880
As Milord has fallen, he requests our allegiance in eradicating the remnants of the Oda clan. {until toaru}

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:19.590
Which of these be of truth?!

00:20:19.590 --> 00:20:22.260
Does Milord live, or not?!

00:20:23.230 --> 00:20:28.950
'Twas these very eyes which beheld the sight of Honno Temple.

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:30.010
Then...

00:20:30.010 --> 00:20:34.270
I believe General Hashiba was misinformed over Milord's whereabouts.

00:20:36.760 --> 00:20:38.500
Perhaps... {arui wa}

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:43.530
he sent this letter, after having learned of Milord's passing.

00:20:44.870 --> 00:20:47.030
Were Milord to have survived the coup, {until nara}

00:20:48.540 --> 00:20:51.460
none would dare to serve Akechi.

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:58.500
Under the pretense of avenging Milord, General Hashiba may attempt to rule the realm.

00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:04.060
I despise the deceptive methods of General Hashiba.

00:21:04.060 --> 00:21:08.560
'Twould be wisest to serve General Akechi.

00:21:08.560 --> 00:21:10.210
However...

00:21:10.210 --> 00:21:14.890
for sending reinforcements, General Hashiba sent a gift worth 600 koku.

00:21:16.400 --> 00:21:20.480
'Tis the duty of a true warrior to honor such gratuity.

00:21:23.180 --> 00:21:26.280
Brother received a gift worth 600 koku?

00:21:28.420 --> 00:21:32.240
His gratitude to ye for sending assistance. {until orei}

00:21:32.240 --> 00:21:36.080
These gifts are said to be worth 1000 koku.

00:21:38.770 --> 00:21:41.810
Received 400 koku fewer than my own!

00:21:42.490 --> 00:21:44.980
And, 'twas a Bizen tea bowl!

00:21:48.300 --> 00:21:51.680
Brother is moreso an accomplished warrior than myself, and yet...

00:21:52.720 --> 00:21:56.090
General Hashiba holds me in higher esteem?!

00:21:56.980 --> 00:22:05.490
To my fellow, Furuta Sasuke, be well in health. {until 2nd time}

00:22:17.540 --> 00:22:20.880
Brother, 'tis General Hashiba whom we shall serve.

00:22:21.290 --> 00:22:25.630
Though General Akechi be refined in warfare, he remains a rebel!

00:22:25.630 --> 00:22:28.320
'Twould be ill-advised to serve a rebel!

00:22:29.070 --> 00:22:33.560
Ye who stress wisdom would dare not serve one so unwise as to rebel!

00:22:33.940 --> 00:22:39.670
Were ye to serve him, ye shall die a death worthy of a true warrior, regardless!

00:22:49.650 --> 00:22:54.080
Though that Bizen tea bowl be a glazed abomination,

00:22:54.970 --> 00:22:58.680
I've not strayed with whom to serve!

00:24:35.760 --> 00:24:37.340
<b> You fool! {purple ts}</b>

00:24:42.610 --> 00:24:44.270
<b>  Behold, the visage of a survivor {blue ts}</b>

00:24:47.360 --> 00:24:48.980
<b> Heart? {green ts}</b>

00:24:50.200 --> 00:24:52.710
White Castle Blues.

00:24:53.300 --> 00:24:58.140
Does the fork joining the aesthete and warrior exist?

00:24:56.570 --> 00:24:59.940
<b> White Castle Blues {ts}</b>
